{ The rooks are gone. Can a pawn sacrifice pull his king away and free your king side? } 10... e3 { Your pawn sacrifice deflects his king and opens a capture on g4. [%cal Ge4e3] } (10... h5 { That loses. The wing push comes before the central deflection. } 11. gxh5 { Taking h5 removes your pawn partner; taking f5 also wins for White. [%cal Rg4h5] }) 11. Kxe3 { He removes the more advanced pawn on e3 rather than taking on f5. } 11... fxg4 { You remove his g pawn and create connected passed pawns. [%cal Gf5g4] } (11... h5 { That loses. The white pawn on g4 can still take your h pawn. } 12. gxh5 { He removes the h pawn instead of taking f5. Your connected-pawn plan is gone. [%cal Rg4h5] }) 12. Kf4 { His king comes back to the king side. } 12... h5 { Your h pawn supports g4. The two passers can help each other advance. [%cal Gh7h5] } (12... g3 { That only draws. The g pawn runs ahead without support. } 13. Kxg3 { His king takes the pawn. Advance its neighbor first to keep the win. [%cal Rf4g3] }) 0-1


