{ Stalemate can save a rook ending. Move your rook to c7 and prepare the sacrifice. [%cal Yc8c7] } 1... Rc7 { You keep the rook ready to check along the seventh rank. [%cal Gc8c7] } (1... Rxc6+ { That loses. Your rook captures on c6. } 2. Rxc6 { White wins your rook, without a stalemate. Keep the rook ready for the d7 sacrifice. [%cal Rc2c6] }) 2. Rg2 { White brings the rook over. Put your rook on d7 with check and offer it to the pawn. [%cal Yc7d7] } 2... Rd7+ { Check! Your rook offers itself where the pawn can capture it. [%cal Gc7d7] } (2... Kc8 { That loses immediately: your king walks into a mating net. } 3. Rg8# { Mate! His rook seals the back row, and his pawn on c6 covers the squares beside your king. [%cal Rg2g8] }) 3. cxd7 { Stalemate! Your king on d8 has no legal move and is not in check, so the game is drawn. [%csl Gd8] } 0-1


