{ A rook-pawn fortress traps the king. Move your king to c4 and attack the pawn. [%cal Yd3c4] } 1... Kc4 { You attack the pawn instead of chasing its king. [%cal Gd3c4] } (1... Ke3 { That loses. Your king goes to e3. } 2. Kb5 2... Kd4 3. a4 { This lets White's king off the rook column to escort the pawn through. Keep that exit shut. [%cal Ra2a4] }) 2. a4 { The pawn advances. Move your king to c5 to keep the exit closed. [%cal Yc4c5] } 2... Kc5 { You keep the king on the rook file. [%cal Gc4c5] } (2... Kd4 { That loses. Your king goes to d4. } 3. Kb5 3... Ke5 4. Kc5 { White slips off the rook file and walks the pawn home. Hold the exit closed instead. [%cal Rb5c5] }) 3. a5 { The pawn advances again. Move your king to c6 for the opposition. [%cal Yc5c6] } 3... Kc6 { You hold his king on the a column. Follow him up the c column and the rook pawn draws. [%cal Gc5c6] } (3... Kd5 { This loses. Your king tries d5. } 4. Kb6 4... Kd6 5. a6 { Letting him off the rook column costs the fortress. Keep the exit closed. [%cal Ra5a6] }) 0-1


