{ His bishop cannot control h1. Can you remove the other passer and reach that corner? } 3. Nxf2 { You give the knight to remove the dangerous f pawn. [%cal Ge4f2] } (3. Nd6 { That loses. Your knight leaves the dangerous f pawn alive. } 3... f1=Q+ 4. Ke4 { Black promotes. Remove the f pawn before heading for the fortress. [%cal Rd3e4] }) 3... Kxf2 { He uses the king. Taking with the bishop also leaves the wrong-colored bishop. } 4. Kd2 { Head for h1. His dark-squared bishop cannot drive your king from that corner, and the position is a draw. [%cal Gd3d2] } (4. Kc2 { Also draws. Your king goes to c2. } 4... Ba5 { Also draws. Your king still reaches h1, a corner the bishop cannot cover. [%cal Bb6a5] }) (4. Kc3 { Also draws. Your king goes to c3. } 4... Kf3 { This holds too. The bishop cannot control h1, and your king still gets there. [%cal Bf2f3] }) (4. Kc4 { Also draws. Your king goes to c4. } 4... Ke2 { Still a draw: h1 is out of the bishop's reach, and your king arrives in time. [%cal Bf2e2] }) (4. Ke4 { Also draws. Your king has time to return toward h1. } 4... Kg3 { This route holds too. Your retreat makes the route to the safe corner easier to see. [%cal Bf2g3] }) 1-0
